{{Codex|The Bronco is a small-scale shotgun that can be wielded with one hand. Only effective at close range, it has a limited clip size.}}
The '''Bronco''' functions like a cross between a shotgun and handgun, that comes in a handy package to complement long range primary weapons.

This weapon can be sold for {{cc|5,000}}; it is also a [[weapon crafting ingredient]] for {{Weapon|Akbronco}} (x2).
{{Checklist|nocategory=true|
* {{Weapon|Bronco}} + {{Weapon|Bronco}} → {{Weapon|Akbronco}}
}}

==Characteristics==
*This weapon deals primarily {{D|Impact}} damage.
*Can use the Bronco-exclusive {{M|Dizzying Rounds}} mod.

{{Advantages|class=Shotgun Sidearm|
*High overall [[status chance]].
*Innate [[multishot]] of 7 pellets.
*Very ammo efficient.
}}

{{Disadvantages|class=Shotgun Sidearm|
*Linear damage falloff from 100% to 75% from 7m to 14m target distance (distances are affected by [[Projectile Speed]]).
*Extremely small magazine size of just 2 rounds; requires frequent reloading.
*Wide pellet spread cone makes the weapon ineffective beyond short range.
}}

{{WeaponComparison|Akbronco}}
{{WeaponComparison|Bronco Prime|header=n}}

==Acquisition==
The Bronco's blueprint can be purchased from the [[Market]].

{{BuildAutomatic|type=Weapon}}

==Incarnon Genesis==
{{Transclude|Bronco Incarnon Genesis#Acquisition}}

{{Transclude|Bronco Incarnon Genesis#Incarnon Genesis}}

==Tips==
*The weapon's spread cone can be shrunken by zooming in.
*It is surprisingly effective at dealing damage over groups of enemies, in close to mid range fights.
**Using maxed {{M|Seeker|Seeker}} is recommended to upgrade its crowd controlling capability, making it the best scatter-damaging sidearm.
==Trivia==
*The word ''Bronco'' is a term in a Spanish Dialect meaning "rough".
**It is also a common term for ''wild horse'' in Western culture.

*Its appearance is similar to the Mauler shotgun-pistol from Halo.
