===Gathering Tips===
''These are based on opinions and may not be true. These should be viewed as advice unless proven undoubtedly true. Check comments for confirmation. Results may vary.''
*When trying to '''actively acquire the Brakk''', first check your profile to see if you have a [[Grustrag Three]] [[Death Mark|mark]] &mdash; You should be able to see it in your profile on the bottom right under: "Marked for Death by:". If you do not, play 5 consecutive missions of a Grineer vs Corpus [[Invasion]] siding with the Corpus (fighting Grineer). After you have completed the missions, you will receive a message from [[Vay Hek|Councilor Vay Hek]] notifying you of being marked.
**Once marked: Play [[Ceres|Lex, Ceres]] &ndash; recommended since it has both [[Orokin Cell]]s and is a Grineer mission &ndash; for 5 minutes exactly, then extract. The Grustrag Three do not spawn past 5 minutes. Feel free to get Orokin Cells by roaming the map waiting for the timer to run out, which you can check by holding tab for mission time. Having multiple party members with the Grustrag Three mark improves chances; although, everyone should be able to get the loot even if only one person has a mark. 
**The Grustrag Three will spawn after enough runs. Use {{WF|Nekros}}' {{A|Desecrate}} ability for a better chance at getting the part you want. Dying can fail the mission unless you have a party member who is also marked. In which case, you will have 50% less damage against Grineer and your party member can still fight the Three. If the mark is consumed, do 5 more Grineer vs Corpus Invasions siding with Corpus until marked again. This can be doing the same mission from 3/3 to 8/3 supporting Corpus and so on.<sup>[Unconfirmed: {{WF|Hydroid}}'s [[Pilfering Swarm]] ability may improve chances of acquiring Brakk parts.]</sup>
*Alternatively you can use the [[Grustrag Three Beacon]] to force them to spawn in.

